<title>TURKEY: TURK DEMIRBANK H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TURK DEMIRBANK H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>					 H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>					 -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	645.63  vs     739.73</p>
<p>    Net Profit		    10,652.88  vs   4,068.51</p>
<p>    Net interest income	 32,390.14  vs  16,971.89</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense  20,741.91  vs  12,118.55</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	    0  vs	26.55</p>
<p>    Loans extended		82,759.07  vs  27,709.37</p>
<p>    Deposits		     136,890.06  vs  41,989.44</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		47,070.43  vs  17,062.62</p>
<p>    Equity			  20,270.62  vs   7,582.59</p>
<p>    Capital			 16,500.00  vs   5,500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Demirbank TAS whose shares are also listed on the Munich bourse, is owned 72.58 percent by Turkish Cingilli Holding AS.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>Demirbank recently said it planned to raise the number of its domestic branches to 71 by end-1997 from current 41.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
